One way to improve the performance of your C# code is to avoid calling a DB stored procedure from a loop. Instead, you can use `SqlBulkCopy`, as suggested by Jamez on Stack Overflow. The `SqlBulkCopy` class provides a high-performance way to bulk insert data into a SQL Server database.

Here's an example of how you can modify your code to use `SqlBulkCopy`:

```csharp
void exEquityCurveMT()
{
    DeletePreviousResultsFromTable("Result_EquityCurve");

    Spliter[] split = MTSplitter(Account.EquityHistory.Count);
    MultiThreadToDataBase[] mtDB = new MultiThreadToDataBase[NUMCORES];

    Task[] taskDB = new Task[NUMCORES];
    for (int i = 0; i < taskDB.Length; i++)
    {
        List<structEquity> eqyList = Account.EquityHistory.GetRange((int)split[i].rowStart, split[i].numRows);
